#! mathcas 2 notebook

#% title
# symbol

#% text
# `symbol(name)` gives the symbol whose name is the string `name`.

#% section
# Details

#% item
# `symbol(name)` is the symbol the reader makes of the name, so `symbol("x") === x`.

#% item
# A string that is not a single name (a keyword, a number, an expression) gives `failure(argument, symbol, 1)`.

#% section
# Examples

#% subsection
# Basic examples

#% cell
symbol("x17")
#% output
#= x17

#% cell
symbol("x17") === x17
#% output
#= true

#% cell
symbol_name(symbol("y32"))
#% output
#= "y32"

#% cell
symbol("1 + 2")
#% output
#! failure(argument, symbol, 1)

#% section
# See also

#% text
# `symbol_name`, `to_expression`, `is_symbol`
